# Software Definition — Hengshi Design v1

This directory defines approved product boundaries, AI tooling, and delivery
workflow for the Hengshi Design platform. Start with the
[visual walkthrough](definition-walkthrough.html) to see the intended experience;
use the [reconciliation map](04-reconciliation-map.md) to find each controlling
definition and its remaining obligations. Approval comes from the durable authority
records, not from either navigation page.

## Documents

| # | Document | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| 01 | [System Boundaries](01-system-boundaries.md) | Protected prototype, approved target, and surface separation |
| 02 | [AI Dev Tooling and MCP](02-ai-dev-tooling-and-mcp.md) | Tool inventory, verified states, and safe fallbacks |
| 03 | [Autonomous AI Development Workflow](03-autonomous-ai-development-workflow.md) | Phase states, approval gates, tool order, and evidence rules |
| 04 | [Reconciliation map](04-reconciliation-map.md) | Canonical subjects, legacy successors and remaining Phase 1 obligations |
| 05 | [Consolidated scope](05-consolidated-goal.md) | Scope carried by the active app goal; no separate goal scheduler |
| 06 | [Entity and public contact](06-entity-and-public-contact.md) | Editable company facts, certificate precision and separate contact channels; [typed shape review](../phase-1-architecture/contracts/reviews/company-facts-shape-2026-10-04.md) passes its bounded inputs, with verification, disclosure and actual admin/publication enforcement still held |
| Visual | [Definition walkthrough](definition-walkthrough.html) | Browser review of the journey, campus direction, departments, staff consultation flow and honest checkpoint |

The map, consolidated scope and visual walkthrough are reconciliation/review
material. They reference accepted decisions and proposed detailed definitions;
they do not accept the complete Phase 1 package or replace approved UI screens.

