The walkthrough explains the system and shows no live staff, functioning console
or operational mailbox. A static viewer is separate from the application servers.
Schema-tooling checks and documentation validation do not prove application behavior.
Review receipts keep their exact input hashes; later reference edits link preserved
bytes without replacing those identities. The
[README inspected by the publication HTTP review](../../output/research/contract-review-reference-reconciliation-2026-10-04/software-definition-README.pre-navigation.md)
is preserved separately from this navigation update.

D-076 settles visitor conversation expiry at 30 minutes of inactivity or an
explicit authorized End, with no absolute conversation duration. The later
[visitor activity and control proposal](../phase-1-architecture/contracts/PRIVATE_PROCESS_PROOF.md#access-lifetime-retention-and-pending-cleanup)
and [human consultation timing amendment](../phase-1-architecture/contracts/HANDOFF_LIFECYCLE.md#timing-conflict-requiring-a-scoped-decision)
are written but not independently reviewed; the earlier PASS receipts above
remain limited to their frozen inputs. The [updated timing panel](definition-walkthrough.html#consultation-sessions)
explains that distinction and keeps staff authentication clocks separate.

The [EU privacy/retention proposal](../phase-1-architecture/contracts/SECURITY_PRIVACY_CONTRACT.md#eu-privacy-and-retention-policy-proposal--2026-10-07)
and its [visual explanation](definition-walkthrough.html#privacy-policy) are also
awaiting independent legal/security review. New purposes and periods are proposals,
not one universal GDPR schedule or live enforcement. Current founder authority
[defers public registration details and the supplied registered address](06-entity-and-public-contact.md);
non-sensitive local data is synthetic, and real production records are supplied
through the intended admin workflow later. Alias ownership remains undecided.
Desktop/narrow-width browser checks validate presentation only; neither the
amendments nor the walkthrough accept the integrated Phase 1 package.

## Durable Authority Bridge

Read and apply these sources in order:

1. `AGENTS.md` and `.specify/memory/constitution.md` for operating and governance
   rules.
2. `PROJECT.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, and `PROJECT_STATE.yaml` for approved product
   intent, decisions, and current phase.
3. This directory for approved product-level definitions.
4. Approved feature artifacts under `specs/` for feature-level requirements,
   research, data models, contracts, plans, and tasks.
5. Source code, tests, and live observations as evidence of current behavior.

Approved decisions outrank approved requirements. The constitution contains the
complete conflict-resolution order.

## Related Documentation

| Document | Authority in the current reset |
|---|---|
| `docs/PROJECT_RULES.md` | Binding project rules |
| `TASKS.md`, `RISKS.md`, `MANUAL_ACTIONS.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` | Durable execution records |
| `docs/decisions-log.md` | Detailed decisions and ADR evidence |
| `docs/active/Hengshi_Design_SRS_v3.md` | Prototype/historical evidence pending Phase 1 reconciliation |
| `docs/active/Hengshi_Design_SAD_v3.md` | Prototype/historical evidence pending Phase 1 reconciliation |
| [Historical security plan](../active/Security_Hardening_Plan.md) | Preserved February proposal, with a [bounded authority-notice review](reviews/legacy-security-authority-v1-2026-10-05.md). The current security contract and v1 feature control; historical scores, packages, thresholds and sprint actions are not current requirements or an executable plan. |
| `docs/active/API_Reference.md` | Current implementation evidence; verify against live OpenAPI |
| `docs/SPEC.md` and `docs/BACKLOG.md` | Legacy prototype scope/task evidence pending reconciliation |

The February 2026 consolidation and “active” documents MUST NOT override the
founder-approved master plan, current v1 constitution, or approved durable decisions.
They remain preserved so Phase 1 can supersede individual claims transparently
instead of deleting history.

D-068–D-070 carry the founder's 2026-10-04 amendments: Azure/AWS deployment
selection and cost planning are deferred; Outlook/Teams remain intended without
a Microsoft 365 prerequisite; Europe is the first market; company facts are
admin-editable reviewed content, with separate privacy/security aliases to be
created by the founder; their ownership stays undecided. These are current authority over historical candidates,
not proof of operational mailboxes, API entitlements or a deployment selection.
Use v1 for the current product/definition; keep factual technical and historical
identifiers intact. Individually newest dependency observations do not select a
stack: select and verify the latest mutually compatible stable graph.

## How This Directory Works

1. Agents read this README after the root governance and state records.
2. Product definitions are revised and reviewed through the material phase loop.
3. Feature-level specifications refine, but cannot silently contradict, approved
   product decisions.
4. Exact dependency versions remain in the dated compatibility matrix and
   lockfiles, not in timeless product rules.
5. Application development remains closed until the complete Phase 1 package is
   founder-approved.
